   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">Employers and Workers organizations signed a framework agreement for establishing National Bipartite Forum for Social Dialogue &#x2013; for strengthening the collaboration of the social partners for decent work and productivity promotion in the country regular through social dialogue and cooperation.
On 17 August 2022, with the support of the ILO, representatives of the Chamber of Commerce and Industry of Timor-Leste (CCI-TL) and the Trade Union Confederation (KSTL), the employers&#x2019; and workers&#x2019; organizations of Timor-Leste, signed the Framework Agreement to establish the National Bipartite Forum for Social Dialogue, aimed at strengthening the collaboration of the social partners for decent work and productivity promotion in the country.
The first of its kind, the Agreement aims to promote trust, collaboration and strengthen the relations between CCI-TL and KSTL members both at the enterprise and national levels through regular social dialogue. It marks the beginning of stronger and sounder bipartite collaboration between Timor-Leste&#x2019;s employers&#x2019; and workers&#x2019; organizations. https://www.ilo.org/jakarta/info/public/pr/WCMS_854163/lang--en/index.htm  follow the b up needed to help constituents to move forward on operationalising the agreement. ILO has been supporting social dialogue among constituents in Timor Leste to address development challenges posed by the pandemic and to build collaborative labour relations for recovery and growth; AS part of this, ILO has supported tripartite and bipartite reviews and capacity building on social dialogue, workplace consultation and cooperation mechanisms and dispute resolution mechanisms.</narrative>
   </description>
